    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Two-Number Calculator\n\nA retro pixel-styled calculator that performs basic arithmetic on two numbers. Works fully offline with no dependencies.\n\n## Features\n\n- Inputs for left and right numbers (supports negative and decimal values)\n- Operation selector: add, subtract, multiply, divide\n- Calculate button to compute the result\n- Output displays only the numeric result, or the exact text `Error` for invalid input\n- Rejects empty inputs, non-finite numbers, and division by zero\n- Keyboard accessible with labeled controls\n- Responsive layout from 360px wide\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter a number in the **Left Number** field.\n3. Choose an operation from the dropdown.\n4. Enter a number in the **Right Number** field.\n5. Click **Calculate** (or press Tab to the button and press Enter/Space).\n6. The result appears in the output area.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- No packages, network requests, or external assets\n- No storage or server code\n- Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript only\n- Under 200 lines total\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — complete app (structure, styles, and logic)\n- `README.md` — this file",
